+/-!
+# `f32`
+
+The pinned Aeneas Lean backend prints the Rust type `f32` as the bare Lean name `F32` (`float_name`
+in `src/extract/ExtractBase.ml`, the `Lean` case of which is `format_of_string "F%d"`) and declares
+no float type anywhere in `Aeneas.Std`, so an extracted fragment that mentions `f32` does not
+elaborate: every occurrence reports `Unknown identifier 'F32'`. This module is the declaration that
+closes that gap.
+
+The representation is the 32-bit payload and nothing else. The model carries no operation on `f32`,
+so `core::f32::f32::is_finite` and the Q32 → `f32` conversions stay `axiom`s of the extracted
+fragment and are audited there as admitted boundary items. There is no arithmetic, no rounding and
+no ordering here, so a value is a bit pattern; anything that needs the numeric meaning of a `f32`
+must be proved against that meaning in the corpus, not read off this structure.
+-/
+
+namespace Aeneas
+
+namespace Std
+
+/-- The IEEE 754 binary32 type, as its 32-bit payload. -/
+structure F32 where
+  /-- The binary32 payload: the 32 bits `f32::to_bits` returns. -/
+  bits : BitVec 32
+  deriving BEq, DecidableEq, Inhabited
+
+end Std
+
+end Aeneas
